<%# The API puts the "Trending Articles" in order from the Plausible analytics, at request time, %>
<%# and the live-update controller puts them here. It removes them when no article is trending. %>
<%# `url`, which is a necessary local, is the API endpoint. %>
<%#
    ⚠️ This section is for the home page and for a Page ONLY. An entry page does not show it, on
    purpose: that page already has "More Reports From This Race", "You May Also Like", and the
    Previous and Next cards, and a fourth list of articles was too much. A Page cannot show "You
    May Also Like", because that section comes from the embeddings of an entry. Thus the trending
    list is the recirculation of a Page.
%>
<%= partial 'partials/placeholders/article_collection', locals: { section_id: 'trending-articles', heading: 'Trending Articles', url: url } %>
